2026-09-14T10:18:37.4412909Z       "body": "### Description\n\nWhen a `BaseModel` dependency contains a complex field annotated with `Query()`, such as `Annotated[list[str] | None, Query()] = None`, repeated query values are not parsed into the model.\n\nPydantic removes the `Annotated` metadata from the generated `inspect.signature`, so FastAPI re-infers the list field as a request body parameter. A request such as `?field=foo&field=bar` therefore produces `field=None`.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```python\nfrom typing import Annotated\nfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, Query\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass Params(BaseModel):\n    field: Annotated[list[str] | None, Query()] = None\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\ndef read(params: Annotated[Params, Depends()]):\n    return params.model_dump()\n\nresponse = TestClient(app).get(\"/?field=foo&field=bar\")\nassert response.json() == {\"field\": [\"foo\", \"bar\"]}\n```\n\n### Solution\n\n- Resolve annotations for `BaseModel` dependency callables with `get_type_hints(..., include_extras=True)`.\n- Preserve the original `Query()` metadata during dependency parameter analysis.\n- Add a regression test covering repeated list-valued query parameters.\n\n### Verification\n\n`python -m pytest tests/test_query_cookie_header_model_extra_params.py tests/test_dependency_class.py tests/test_dependency_models.py -q`\n\n30 passed in 0.58s.\n\n`ruff check` and `ruff format --check` both pass.",
